The vector $\underset{\sim}{a}$ is shown on the grid.
Find $4\underset{\sim}{a}$ as a column vector.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[help lines] (-1,-3) grid (4,2);
\draw[->] (-1,0) -- (4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,2) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (3,-2) node[midway,above right] {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

On the grid, $\underset{\sim}{v}$ and $\underset{\sim}{w}$ are drawn.
Write $\underset{\sim}{w}$ in terms of $\underset{\sim}{v}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[help lines] (-4,-1) grid (3,4);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (2,1) node[midway,below right] {$\underset{\sim}{v}$};
\draw[->,thick] (1,3) -- (-3,1) node[midway,above] {$\underset{\sim}{w}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The vector $\underset{\sim}{c}$ is shown on the grid.
Sketch $\frac{1}{2}\underset{\sim}{c}$ on the grid.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[help lines] (-1,-1) grid (5,2);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (4,0) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{c}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

foundation.solution_text:
The scalar $\frac{1}{2}$ is positive, so keep the direction and halve the length. One correct sketch is shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[help lines] (-1,-1) grid (5,2);
\draw[->,thick] (0,0) -- (4,0) node[midway,below] {$\underset{\sim}{c}$};
\draw[->,thick] (0,1) -- (2,1) node[midway,above] {$\frac{1}{2}\underset{\sim}{c}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

